{
    "name": "personal-data-hub",
    "description": "A secure and user-friendly desktop application for managing personal data, built with Electron and Next.js.",
    "displayName": "Personal Data Hub",
    "license": "MIT",
    "repository": {
        "type": "git",
        "url": "https://github.com/your-username/personal-data-hub.git"
    },
    "keywords": [
        "personal data",
        "data management",
        "electron",
        "next.js",
        "desktop application",
        "secure storage"
    ],
    "readme": "# Personal Data Hub\n\nPersonal Data Hub is a secure and user-friendly desktop application for managing your personal data. Built with Electron and Next.js, it provides a seamless experience for organizing, storing, and accessing your sensitive information.\n\n## Features\n\n- **Secure Storage**: Encrypt your data using industry-standard encryption techniques to ensure your information is safe.\n- **User-Friendly Interface**: A clean and intuitive interface that makes it easy to manage your personal data.\n- **Cross-Platform**: Available on Windows, macOS, and Linux.\n- **Data Organization**: Categorize and tag your data for easy retrieval.\n- **Backup and Sync**: Option to backup your data locally or sync with cloud services (coming soon).\n\n## Installation\n\n1. Clone the repository:\n   ```bash\n   git clone",
    "version": "1.1.2-1",
    "private": true,
    "main": "./electron/main.js",
    "author": {
        "name": "Prashant Acharya",
        "email": "prashant_acharya@yahoo.com"
    },
    "scripts": {
        "next-dev": "next dev -p 4000",
        "electron-dev": "cross-env NODE_ENV=development wait-on http://localhost:4000 && nodemon --watch electron --ext js --exec \"electron ./electron/main.js\"",
        "dev": "concurrently \"npm run next-dev\" \"npm run electron-dev\"",
        "build": "next build",
        "start": "next start -p 4000",
        "dist:mac": "npm run build && electron-builder --mac",
        "dist:linux": "npm run build && electron-builder --linux",
        "dist:win": "npm run build && electron-builder --win",
        "postinstall": "electron-rebuild -f -w keytar"
    },
    "build": {
        "asar": false,
        "appId": "com.personal.data",
        "productName": "Personal Data Hub",
        "files": [
            "electron/**/*",
            "database/**/*",
            "help/**/*",
            "out/**/*",
            "package.json"
        ],
        "mac": {
            "target": [
                "dmg",
                "zip"
            ],
            "category": "public.app-category.productivity",
            "identity": null,
            "icon": "build/icon.icns"
        },
        "linux": {
            "target": [
                "AppImage",
                "deb"
            ],
            "category": "Utility",
            "icon": "build/icon.png",
            "executableName": "personal-data-hub"
        },
        "win": {
            "icon": "build/icon.ico",
            "target": [
                "nsis"
            ]
        },
        "extraResources": [
            {
                "from": "database/",
                "to": "database/"
            }
        ]
    },
    "dependencies": {
        "bcryptjs": "^3.0.3",
        "better-sqlite3": "^12.9.0",
        "better-sqlite3-multiple-ciphers": "^12.9.0",
        "crypto": "^1.0.1",
        "crypto-js": "^4.2.0",
        "docx": "^9.6.1",
        "keytar": "^7.9.0",
        "lowdb": "^1.0.0",
        "marked": "^18.0.3",
        "next": "16.2.3",
        "qrcode": "^1.5.4",
        "react": "19.2.4",
        "react-dom": "19.2.4",
        "recharts": "^3.8.1",
        "speakeasy": "^2.0.0",
        "uuid": "^13.0.0"
    },
    "devDependencies": {
        "@electron/rebuild": "^4.0.4",
        "babel-plugin-react-compiler": "1.0.0",
        "concurrently": "^9.2.1",
        "cross-env": "^10.1.0",
        "electron": "^41.2.0",
        "electron-builder": "^25.1.8",
        "electron-rebuild": "^3.2.9",
        "eslint": "^9",
        "eslint-config-next": "16.2.3",
        "nodemon": "^3.1.14",
        "wait-on": "^9.0.4"
    }
}
